.TH STOP-DARPA-SPILLSERVER 1 "September 24, 2026" "darpa_spillserver 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stop-darpa-spillserver \- stop a DARPA Spill Information Server started from a checkout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./stop\-darpa\-spillserver.sh
.PP
.B .\e stop\-darpa\-spillserver.ps1
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stops a server started by
.BR start-darpa-spillserver (1).
It reads the PID file and checks that the PID is still a
.B darpa\-spill\-server
process \(em by its command line, so a stale file never stops an unrelated
process. If not, it removes the stale PID file and exits 0.
.PP
On Linux and macOS it sends
.BR SIGTERM ,
which lets uvicorn finish in-flight requests and the poller close the SQLite
archive cleanly, and waits up to the grace period. If the process is still
there it sends
.BR SIGKILL .
.PP
On Windows a windowless console process has no equivalent of
.BR SIGTERM ,
so the stop is a hard terminate
.RB ( "taskkill /T /F" ,
which also ends the Python child the console-script launcher starts). It then
waits up to 15 s for the process to go.
.PP
A hard stop is safe: the archive is in SQLite WAL mode, so at most the last
poll is lost, and the next poll's overlap re-reads it.
.PP
The PID file is removed once the process has gone.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SPILL_PIDFILE
PID file. Default
.IR run/spillserver.pid .
.TP
.B SPILL_GRACE
(sh) Seconds to wait after
.B SIGTERM
before
.BR SIGKILL .
Default \fB15\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The server was stopped, or was not running.
.TP
.B 1
The process survived the kill.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.EX
\&./stop\-darpa\-spillserver.sh
SPILL_GRACE=60 ./stop\-darpa\-spillserver.sh
.EE
.RE
.PP
On Windows:
.PP
.RS
.EX
\&.\e stop\-darpa\-spillserver.ps1
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-darpa-spillserver (1),
.BR darpa-spill-server (1)
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report defects at
\fBhttps://github.com/NovaDAQ/DARPA\-SpillServer/issues\fR.
.SH AUTHOR
NOvA DAQ group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
